 ## Overview
-Manifold Dual Marching Cubes (Manifold DualMC) is a surface extraction algorithm that generates a topologically correct, manifold mesh from a voxel grid by resolving the ambiguous configurations (C16 and C19) inherent in standard Dual Marching Cubes [S2, S4, unofficial]. While standard Dual Marching Cubes places vertices at dual points (face centers) to ensure a manifold surface, it fails to handle specific cell configurations where the topology of the isosurface crossing a face is ambiguous, potentially leading to non-manifold vertices or edges [S4, unofficial]. Manifold DualMC solves this by precomputing a lookup table that maps these problematic configurations to their ambiguous face direction, allowing the algorithm to check neighboring cells and invert the cell code when necessary to ensure consistent manifold connectivity [S2, S4, unofficial]. It differs from standard Dual Marching Cubes by explicitly handling these ambiguous cases to guarantee a watertight mesh [S4, unofficial].
+Manifold Dual Marching Cubes (Manifold DualMC) is a surface extraction algorithm that generates a topologically correct, manifold mesh from a voxel grid by resolving the ambiguous configurations (C16 and C19) inherent in standard Dual Marching Cubes [S2, S3, unofficial]. While standard Dual Marching Cubes places vertices at dual points (face centers) to ensure a manifold surface, it fails to handle specific cell configurations where the topology of the isosurface crossing a face is ambiguous, potentially leading to non-manifold vertices or edges [S3, unofficial]. Manifold DualMC solves this by precomputing a lookup table that maps these problematic configurations to their ambiguous face direction, allowing the algorithm to check neighboring cells and invert the cell code when necessary to ensure consistent manifold connectivity [S2, S3, unofficial]. It differs from standard Dual Marching Cubes by explicitly handling these ambiguous cases to guarantee a watertight mesh [S3, unofficial].
 
